# Cursor previous / next

Previous loads the page before the current `startCursor`. It does not reload page one.

Relay keeps a fragment's default `first` when a refetch passes `first: null` (`relay-runtime` `getOperationVariables` only overrides a default when the value is non-null). A Previous request therefore arrives as `first: <default>`, `last: <page size>`, `before: <start cursor>`.

`cursor.NewCursor` honors `before` over `first`, and `after` over `last`. Do not add a resolver branch that uses `first` whenever it is set; that drops `before` and returns the first page.

Client previous/next goes through `useCursorPagination`:

- Next: `{ first: pageSize, after: endCursor, last: null, before: null }`
- Previous: `{ first: null, after: null, last: pageSize, before: startCursor }`

Do not change Previous to `first: pageSize` or omit `before`. Select `pageInfo { hasNextPage hasPreviousPage startCursor endCursor }`. Do not use `@connection` / `loadNext` for a previous/next control.

An in-memory list pages with an index into the array. Previous decrements that index. It does not set the index back to 0.

See [`contrib/claude/pagination.md`](../../contrib/claude/pagination.md).
